VALUES ('Wilkes Open', '2025-07-20'::date, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'college-open', '236 S. River St., Wilkes‑Barre, PA 18702', 'Established over 90 years ago and often called the "Rose Bowl of Wrestling," the Wilkes Open is one of the longest-running and most competitive early-season college tournaments in the country. It features a deep and diverse field with NCAA Division I, II, and III programs, along with select unattached high school athletes competing at the elite level.

This open-format tournament provides a rare opportunity for high school standouts to test themselves against seasoned collegiate competition. Past participants have included programs like Appalachian State, Duke, Davidson, Alvernia, Wilkes, and Penn College.

💥 Highly recommended for experienced, nationally competitive wrestlers only.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, false, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, '2025-07-20T19:04:02+00:00'::timestamptz, NOW());

